# Curated archive-jar mappings (requirement 36 of
# dev-support/licenses/License-Management.md).
#
# Jars in the assembled archive that resist automatic g:a normalization —
# shaded jars whose own pom.properties is absent (the enumeration then
# knows only the artifactId from the manifest/filename) or jars with no
# metadata at all. The archive gate (check-archive-licenses.sh) promotes
# matching rows before any check runs; a mapped jar is classified by its
# real group like any other (own org.apache.hadoop jars are exempt from
# third-party checks, everything else must be licensed in LICENSE-binary).
#
# Format: `stem g:a # justification` — stem is the jar filename without
# the version and .jar (the manifest/filename artifactId the enumeration
# reports). The version comes from the jar itself; the mapping pins only
# the identity.
#
# Every entry is confirmed by the next ground-truth run: a mapping whose
# jar stops shipping, or whose stem now resolves automatically, is stale
# and must be pruned.

hadoop-client-runtime org.apache.hadoop:hadoop-client-runtime # shaded client jar: keeps 71 embedded pom.properties but none of its own; our artifact, covered by the archive's top-level Apache LICENSE
